From b10240f196949efc50fb0a80eff156eabbaeb9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:00:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Stances that never stick, flinches that keep a blow, impacts
 that land, the bow's aim line

The hit-stop holds every clip at speed 0 and gives each its speed back, instead of pausing: a
paused main clip that the driver re-armed away from mid-stop is never faded by Bevy's transitions
and played on at full weight once resumed, leaving a swing, block or reel stuck over the gait. A
hit-stop asked again while one runs extends it. Clips replaced (twice in a frame, or the lock-on
shuffle's other foot) release their nodes. A flinch on a body winding up its own blow keeps that
clip and carries the hit in the lean. The action layer's swing results (HitInfo 0x10000) land at
once while an add-on drives it. The camera's unit collision skips dead bodies and passes through
one right behind the head. Aiming while locked on centres the view on the locked unit.
GetActionAim() gives the add-on the view centre's facing and elevation, for a shot along the
reticle's line.
